mission "A Door in the Reef"
    name "A Door in the Reef"
    description "Carry the tideglass to the reef entrance and wait for the moon-pulled current."
    source "Saint's Refuge"
    destination "Mermaid's Rest"
    reward 2045
    speaker offer "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    speaker visit "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    speaker complete "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    to offer
        has "The Battle of Lantern Passage: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Doctor Inez places the tideglass in a padded case. It catches the light whenever the moon shifts above the reef, and the old notes say the current opens a passage only briefly.`
            `Inez checks the tideglass against the moon's position. "Carry this to the reef entrance and wait for the moon-pulled current. It will show us whether the drowned settlement can be reached without breaking a ship against the coral."`
            choice
                `"Fair enough. Give me a heading and I will sail."`
                    accept
                `"What would happen if we leave it alone?"`
                    goto details
                `"I have my own course to keep. Find another ship."`
                    close
            label details
                `She closes the case and hands it to you. "Do not force the passage. Watch the glass and wait for the water to turn; the channel is brief, and a captain who mistakes impatience for courage will lose a vessel."`
                choice
                    `"That settles it. Let us be about it."`
                        accept
                    `"I cannot take this on. Find another captain."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Door in the Reef. Carry the tideglass to the reef entrance and wait for the moon-pulled current."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Mermaid's Rest, Inez checks the tideglass against the current. The moon-pulled flow opens the reef entrance, revealing a route toward the drowned settlement. "It is real," she says. "And it is only open while the sea allows it."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Inez puts the tideglass away. "You have shown us the way in, not the right to take what lies there. That distinction matters. We will bring the councils into this before anyone goes below."`
        log "Completed A Door in the Reef. Received 2045 gold. Carry the tideglass to the reef entrance and wait for the moon-pulled current."
